# winoracle 2026-09-28, WARP (Microsoft Basic Render Driver), FL 11_1, x64.
# (x86 build: identical up to "C fmt 85"; the 32-bit WARP process dies there.)
# Vitreo 2026-09-28 (build of Sep 27 23:22), x64 and x86 identical. Verdicts:
#  A GS assembly, all non-adjacency topologies, strips, cuts (R16/R32),
#    0xFFFF-as-index in R32, LINESTRIP_ADJ/TRIANGLELIST_ADJ/TRIANGLESTRIP_ADJ: CORRECT
#  A LINELIST_ADJ through a GS: WRONG (garbage vertices: "0/0 0/0 0/0 0/-")
#  A SV_VertexID includes StartVertexLocation / BaseVertexLocation: WRONG
#    (spec 8.16: Draw starts at 0; DrawIndexed = the index value)
#  A out-of-range vertex fetch (Draw past VB end, index past end): WRONG
#    (reads the neighbouring allocation, 1000+ -> 2000+; spec 8.19.2: 0)
#  A cut value inside TRIANGLELIST / LINELIST: WRONG (Vitreo drops the
#    primitive holding the cut and keeps index positions; spec 8.12/8.13
#    restart assembly after the cut)
#  B InstanceDataStepRate 0: WRONG (treated as 1; spec 8.3.1: never steps,
#    starts at StartInstanceLocation). Step 1/2/3, strides, offsets: CORRECT
#  B unbound per-instance slot: WRONG (draw skipped; Windows fetches 0)
#  C R16_UNORM/R16_UINT/R16_SNORM/R16_SINT/D16_UNORM: WRONG (vertex format
#    table shifted by one DXGI value); R10G10B10A2_UINT: MISSING;
#    B8G8R8X8/B5G6R5/B5G5R5A1/B4G4R4A4 IA: unsupported (optional);
#    R9G9B9E5 IA: extra (WARP: unsupported). All other formats: CORRECT
#    (SNORM 1-ULP difference within 3.1 division tolerance)
#  D patch lists 1..32 CP: WRONG (nothing drawn: "vertex input-layout
#    specialization failed" for a VS without SV_Position feeding an HS)
#  E adjacency topologies with no GS: WRONG (drawn as TRIANGLELIST of
#    consecutive vertices); leading vertex of lists/strips: CORRECT
#  E rasterized TRIANGLELIST containing the cut: WRONG (see A)
